1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
AbbeyRoad.online is a scheduling site for a university band club. Members open "My schedule".

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:20,000
The member starts the connection with "Connect with Google".

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:45,000
The consent screen requests calendar.events, to read busy times and to add confirmed practices. It also lists calendar.calendarlist.readonly, a non-sensitive scope.

4
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The member grants access.

5
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:15,000
The member chooses which calendars to import, including a secondary calendar. Only the selected calendars are read.

6
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:30,000
One calendar is deselected and the choice is saved.

7
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Events from the selected calendars are read with calendar.events and shown as busy times, so the band can find a free slot.

8
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:15,000
When a practice is confirmed, one event is created on the member's primary calendar with calendar.events.

9
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:35,000
If the practice time changes, only that event is updated. Other events are never touched.

10
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:55,000
When the member disconnects, the access token is revoked and the imported events are deleted.

11
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:05,000
The privacy policy explains how Google user data is used.
